# charon integration step 26 after 546078ea5d: commit fd24718a125dcec228a9fabb6f53087cfa2fb2e9
# first parent d0c1e0b0e83fd83d4b56945ea2fa8d4c20add4d3
# series charon: patch -p1 in charon/ of the upstream source
#
# charon: translate dependency bodies from their exported promoted MIR
#
# Crate metadata only carries the runtime MIR of a dependency (optimized_mir, mir_for_ctfe),
# after runtime lowering: ElaborateBoxDerefs turns `*b` on a Box into projections through
# Unique/NonNull plus a null-pointer UB check, and drops are elaborated. Under --mir=promoted,
# local bodies come from mir_promoted, so the same function translated from a dependency and
# locally differed (e.g. chelis_deep's Expr::carrier failed in Aeneas only when translated from
# chelis-effects).
#
# DependencyCallbacks now also captures the promoted MIR (body and promoted constants) of every
# MIR-carrying definition when rustc computes it (a mir_promoted provider override; bodies no
# analysis forced are built at export) and writes it beside the artifact as
# <artifact>.charon-mir: version header, the crate hash (SVH) of the compilation, and entries
# keyed by definition-path hash. The encoding reuses rustc's TyEncodable/TyDecodable with a codec
# that maps DefIds by DefPathHash, crates by StableCrateId, allocations by content and spans by
# (exported source file id, offset); span hygiene data is not kept, and cross-crate-cleared data
# is cleared as in metadata MIR.
#
# At --mir=promoted, get_mir reads bodies and promoteds of external items from the table of the
# exact artifact rustc loaded, for every crate that is not in the sysroot. A missing table, a
# table with another version or crate hash, or a missing entry is a translation error, never a
# fallback to the runtime MIR. Statics, whose initializer MIR the metadata does not carry, now
# get their promoted body too. The standard library keeps its runtime MIR (the only MIR it
# ships); constructors keep their shim; trivial constants keep their evaluated value. Other MIR
# levels are unchanged.
#
# The UI harness compiles aux crates through charon-driver's dependency mode, as `charon cargo`
# does. New test foreign-box-deref: a dependency's Box derefs, move out of a box, promoted
# constant, static and const fn translate exactly like local copies of the same functions.

